@startuml
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam defaultFontColor #1E293B
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 15
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowColor #94A3B8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #CBD5E1
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #CBD5E1
  BorderThickness 1.5
}

rectangle "EVPN-for-OVN\nReusable Go Framework" as Framework #EAF2FF

together {
  rectangle "Standalone Framework\nconsumer" as Standalone
  rectangle "Kubernetes CNI / Multus\napplication" as Kubernetes
  rectangle "OpenStack Neutron\n(future consumer)" as OpenStack
}

together {
  rectangle "Netlink-Programmed\nFramework integration" as Netlink #EAF6F0
  rectangle "OVSDB-Programmed\nFramework integration" as OVSDB #EAF6F0
  rectangle "GoBGP\nEVPN control plane" as GoBGP #F3F6FA
}
together {
  rectangle "Linux EVPN\nintegration state" as Kernel #FFF7E7
  rectangle "OVN NBDB / OVSDB\nowned route state" as NBDB #FFF7E7
}
rectangle "ovn-controller" as Controller #EAF2FF
rectangle "OVN / OVS\nworkload forwarding" as Forwarding #EAF2FF
rectangle "EVPN overlay /\nremote VTEPs" as Overlay #F3F6FA
rectangle "External FRR peer\n(validation)" as FRR
rectangle "Kubernetes deployment (optional integration layer)" {
  rectangle "BGPConfiguration CRD" as BGPConfig
  rectangle "k8gobgp manager\nKubernetes-native GoBGP management" as BGPManager
  BGPConfig --> BGPManager : reconciliation
}

Standalone --> Framework
Kubernetes --> Framework
OpenStack ..> Framework : future
Framework --> Netlink
Framework --> OVSDB
Framework --> GoBGP : gRPC Type-2 lifecycle
BGPManager --> GoBGP : configuration
Netlink --> Kernel
Kernel --> Controller : observed
OVSDB --> NBDB : Type-2 route import
NBDB --> Controller : OVN reconciliation
Controller --> Forwarding
GoBGP <--> FRR : BGP EVPN routes
Overlay <--> FRR : peer-side VXLAN / workload
Forwarding <..> Overlay : workload traffic
note bottom of BGPManager
  BGP identity / peers / AF / VRFs are CRD-owned.
  Upstream DaemonSet image runs manager + gobgpd.
  Framework owns its Type-2 paths and integration state.
  Non-Kubernetes deployments need no k8gobgp.
end note
@enduml
